# Crypto Watcher — Frontend

> Phase tags (`MVP`, `Phase 1`, `Phase 2`, `Phase 3`, `Final`) cite
> [ROADMAP](./ROADMAP.mdc). The UI consumes the API in [BACKEND](./BACKEND.mdc)
> and reads on-chain data/contracts in [CONTRACTS](./CONTRACTS.mdc). Keep this
> file in sync with the actual `apps/web/` implementation (see the docs-sync rule
> in `.cursor/rules/`).

## Tech Stack

The proposed full-application redesign is tracked in
[REDESIGN_PLAN](./REDESIGN_PLAN.md). Its R0–R8 milestones describe incremental UI
delivery, not changes to the product phases below. Existing behavior remains the
baseline until each milestone is implemented and verified; governance stays `[MVP]`.

From the [README](../README.md): Vite + React + TypeScript + TailwindCSS,
Shadcn/UI (fully rounded, Uber-inspired cream/yellow palette), Zustand, React Hook Form,
React Router, Sonner, Remix Icons, Raleway font. Web3: RainbowKit, Wagmi, Viem.
Tests: Vitest + Testing Library (unit/integration) and Playwright (e2e). Monorepo via Nx + pnpm.

> **Product model:** Official scores come from a vetted governor council. Regular users
> browse reports, comment, submit evidence and participate in protocol governance — but
> do not vote on project risk scores. Legacy project voting UI remains during migration.

