```

### Zustand store slices (`store/`) `[MVP]`

```ts
// store/session.ts
interface SessionState {
  user?: { id: string; walletAddress: string; role: 'user'|'team'|'admin' }
  setUser: (u?: SessionState['user']) => void
}

// modules/voting/store.ts
interface VotingState {
  pendingTxHash?: string
  selectedChoice?: number
  setChoice: (c: number) => void
}
```

> Frontend persistence note: the frontend has no SQL store of its own; persistent
> data is modeled in PostgreSQL on the backend (see the SQL Data Modeling section
> of [BACKEND](./BACKEND.mdc)). The client only keeps cached server data + UI state.

## SEO & performance `[MVP]`

- **`lib/seo/`** — `PageMeta` (react-helmet-async), `RouteSeo` in the app shell,
  `resolveRouteMeta()` for every public route (static + blog + reference projects),
  JSON-LD (WebSite, Organization, Article, Product/Review, BreadcrumbList).
- **Build artifacts** — `pnpm --filter web seo:generate` (also runs before `build`)
  writes `src/public/robots.txt` and `sitemap.xml` from `VITE_SITE_URL` +
  `getIndexablePaths()`. Auth/admin/profile routes are `noindex`.
- **Fonts** — self-hosted via `@fontsource` (no render-blocking Google Fonts).
- **Code splitting** — lazy-loaded route chunks + manual Rollup vendor splits
  (`web3`, `motion`, `query`, `vendor-react`) for Lighthouse performance.

## Conventions

- One module = one folder under `modules/`, owning `components/`, `hooks/`,
  `api/`, `store.ts`, `routes.tsx` and `__tests__/`.
- Use Shadcn/UI primitives from `components/ui/`; do not fork them per feature.
- Global/shared state in Zustand (`store/`); feature state in the feature's slice.
- All network calls through the typed client in `lib/api/`; on-chain calls through
  `lib/web3/`.
- Tests: Vitest + Testing Library in `__tests__/` as `*.test.tsx` only (render
  components/hooks — no plain `*.test.ts` lib unit tests); Playwright e2e in
  `e2e/`. Coverage thresholds in `vite.config.ts`. `[MVP]`
- Browser journeys: `pnpm --filter web test:e2e` builds the app, serves it with
  `vite preview` (API base `/api`) and runs Chromium on desktop and mobile
  viewports. `e2e/fixtures.ts` answers every `/api/*` call from in-memory state and
  aborts all cross-origin requests, so journeys never depend on the database,
  public RPCs or market APIs. CI runs them in the `apps/web` job. `[MVP]`
- Bundle report: `pnpm --filter web exec tsx scripts/report-bundle-size.ts` after a
  build prints raw/gzip sizes per chunk and the initial payload. `[MVP]`
- Lighthouse: `pnpm --filter web lighthouse` builds the app, serves `vite preview`,
  audits public routes from `lighthouse.config.json`, and fails when category
  scores fall below configured thresholds. CI runs this after the web build
  (`pnpm run lighthouse:web`). `[MVP]`
